abstract: >-
  A conditional, covariate-aware Bayesian stepwise framework for
  refining candidate regions in the Gaussian linear mixed model.  At
  each step the candidate-specific marginal likelihood integrates the
  residual variance analytically; the variance-component ratio is
  handled either by a plug-in REML evaluation (REML-BF, the balanced
  default) or by numerical Gauss-Legendre marginalisation (MBF,
  conservative).  The framework subsumes Wakefield's approximate Bayes
  factor as a special case, adds a joint Schur-complement variant that
  stays stable under within-block LD saturation, and controls the
  selected-set size with the extended BIC; covariate adjustment is
  built into the conditioning matrix without modifying the
  Bayes-factor algebra.
keywords:
  - "Bayesian variable selection"
  - "linear mixed model"
  - "Bayes factor"
  - "genetic fine-mapping"
  - "polygenic background"
  - "stepwise selection"
  - "extended BIC"
  - "Gauss-Legendre quadrature"
